                <pb facs="0504" n="406" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg406"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hart to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-08-05"><hi rendition="#italic">August 5,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Hart reports that the Vice-President has taken possession, by a surprise, of
                    the Government and installed a cabinet at Bogotá. The President is unaware of
                    the movement. The Conservative party supports the Vice-President, the President
                    being supported by the National party. The city is quiet.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
